<section id="thesis">
  <div class="wrap rv">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-no">02</span><h2>The research</h2></div>
    <p class="thesis-lede">Can an LLM read a datacenter's logs and tell you which lines matter? My thesis put <em>Claude Sonnet 4.6</em> and <em>Llama 3.1</em> head-to-head against classical ML — at scale, with the failure modes documented.</p>
    <div class="metrics">
      <div class="metric"><div class="num" data-count="93.58"><i>%</i></div><div class="lbl">F1 · TF-IDF + logistic regression baseline</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><div class="num" data-count="99.61"><i>%</i></div><div class="lbl">Accuracy · 115,013 test sequences</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><div class="num" data-count="11"><i>M+</i></div><div class="lbl">HDFS log lines processed</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><div class="num" data-count="20"><i>%</i></div><div class="lbl">LLM hallucination rate found &amp; documented</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="thesis-cols">
      <div>
        <h4>What I built</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>End-to-end Python pipeline — parsing, sessionisation, feature extraction at 11M+ line scale</li>
          <li>TF-IDF + logistic regression baseline, trained and evaluated at scale</li>
          <li>LLM harness via OpenRouter (Claude Sonnet 4.6) and Cerebras (Llama 3.1 8B)</li>
          <li>Zero-shot, few-shot and chain-of-thought prompting, benchmarked side by side</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>What I found</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Classical ML still wins on structured logs — decisively, at a fraction of the cost</li>
          <li>LLMs achieved 100% classification consistency across repeated runs</li>
          <li>…but hallucinated evidence in 20% of explanations — a real risk for SOC workflows</li>
          <li>Context truncation collapsed LLM F1 from 53.33% to 0% — a hard failure mode</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="stackline"><b>Stack</b> — Python · scikit-learn · pandas · OpenRouter API · Cerebras API · LaTeX</p>
  </div>
</section>

